This project uses @hivellm/rulebook standards.

CRITICAL RULES:
1. Always reference @AGENTS.md before coding
2. Write tests first (95%+ coverage required)
3. Run quality checks before committing:
   - Type check / Compiler check
   - Linter (no warnings allowed)
   - All tests (100% pass rate)
   - Coverage check
4. Update docs/ when implementing features
5. Follow strict documentation structure

PLATFORM REQUIREMENT:
Due to Tantivy/WSL compatibility limitations (see docs/WSL_TANTIVY_CONFLICT.md), all builds, tests, and development operations MUST be performed in PowerShell (Windows native), NOT in WSL. This includes:
- Running `cargo build`, `cargo test`, `cargo clippy`
- Executing integration tests
- Running the server for testing
- Any filesystem operations that interact with Tantivy indices

Use Windows native paths (e.g., `C:\Users\...`) instead of WSL paths (`/mnt/f/...`) for data directories.

Language-specific rules are in @AGENTS.md.
Module-specific patterns are in @AGENTS.md.

When in doubt, ask to review @AGENTS.md first.

MCP CONFIGURATION:
The Lexum MCP server is available at http://localhost:17000/mcp
Configuration files are in .cursor/ directory for Cursor IDE integration.
